<!--BlockML Documentation — update A02 page groups
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task.A02_UpdatePageGroups-->
<task:A02_UpdatePageGroups xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that updates A02 page groups
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A02 structuring task: materialize PageGroupPlan entries from BmlDocSetPlan
    into concrete PageGroups under the a02 pagegroup package. Name, title,
    parentGroup, and pages come only from the plan. This task has no
    authoritativeSources.
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          All information for this task comes from the plan. Do not read
          authoritativeSources on this task or on BmlDocSetPlan. Do not invent
          groups, titles, or page membership that the plan does not state.

          1. Read the plan
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a01_planning.data.BmlDocSetPlan. Walk every
          PageGroupPlan under rootPageGroupPlan, including nested groups. For each
          group, collect its direct PagePlan children (pages of that group) and its
          nested PageGroupPlan children (child groups). Do not flatten nested
          groups into the parent’s pages list.

          2. Resolve A02 FQNs
          PageGroup FQN =
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.pagegroup + "." +
          PageGroupPlan.name
          (for example RootPageGroup →
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.pagegroup.RootPageGroup).

          Page FQN =
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page + "." + PagePlan.name
          (for example docs.FirstBlock →
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.FirstBlock).

          Write only under this a02 pagegroup package, never a pagegroup package
          outside a02 (a03 or any later sector). Do not create or edit pages,
          DocSet, or pageMapping. Do not write PageGroups outside a02.

          3. Link only existing a02 pages — fail if a planned page is missing
          For each PagePlan of a group, the matching a02 page must already exist.
          If that a02 page is absent, throw
          org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow.ExecutionException naming the
          PagePlan.name and the expected a02 page FQN. Do not skip the page, do
          not create it here, and do not link a substitute from another sector.
          Only a02 pages may appear in pages. Never link a page outside a02.

          4. Write each PageGroup from the plan
          If a group with that name already exists, discard its current content
          and regenerate the file from the plan. Keep only the FQN / file path so
          the same Block is overwritten. Do not invent groups that are not in the
          plan.

          Each PageGroup must:
          - use baseType org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.PageGroup
          - use PageGroupPlan.name as the Block name
          - override title from PageGroupPlan.title
          - set parentGroup to the A02 FQN of the enclosing PageGroupPlan
            when this group is nested; omit parentGroup on the root
            PageGroupPlan (the root of rootPageGroupPlan has no parent)
          - fill pages with TypeReferenceEntity links to the a02 pages of
            that group’s direct PagePlan children, in plan order
          - omit landingPage unless the plan supplies one (it does not)
          - omit every other aggregation

          Export each A02 PageGroup from org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is
          not already in the catalog. Do not remove catalog entries of other
          sectors.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
</task:A02_UpdatePageGroups>
